 ## [Unreleased]

+### Changed
+
+- **Migration: `ToolRegistry.execute` now validates tool input against `inputSchema` before calling the executor.**
+  A static tool's JSON Schema is compiled at `register` time (throwing synchronously if the schema itself is
+  invalid), and a function-valued tool definition's schema is compiled and cached by schema object reference on
+  each call. When `input` violates `required`, declared property types or `enum`, `execute` logs the failing
+  property paths without logging values and returns a `ToolResponse` describing the violation so the model can
+  correct the call on the next tool round instead of ending the turn with an unhandled error; undeclared extra
+  properties still pass through unchanged without type coercion or injected defaults. An executor that previously
+  hand-validated its arguments now receives only input the declared schema already accepts, so any tool that
+  relied on seeing malformed input to return its own custom error message will no longer be called for those
+  inputs.
+
